  <section id="intro">
    <h2>1. Introduction</h2>
    <p>This Privacy Policy explains how Innca Technologies ("we", "us", "our") collects, uses, and protects information when you use the NIVORA mobile application (the "App"). By creating an account or otherwise using the App, you agree to the practices described here. If you do not agree, please do not use the App.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="who-we-are">
    <h2>2. Who We Are</h2>
    <p>NIVORA is developed and operated by Innca Technologies. For any question about this policy or how your data is handled, contact us at <a href="mailto:support@inncatechnologies.com">support@inncatechnologies.com</a>.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="age">
    <h2>3. Age Requirement</h2>
    <p>NIVORA is intended for users <strong>18 years of age or older</strong>. We do not knowingly collect information from anyone under 18. If we become aware that an account belongs to a minor, we will take steps to delete the associated data.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="info-you-provide">
    <h2>4. Information You Provide</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Account information:</strong> full name, username, and password at registration.</li>
      <li><strong>Onboarding &amp; relationship profile:</strong> your answers about yourself, your relationship, and your partner, collected during onboarding and in the Customize section.</li>
      <li><strong>Profile photo:</strong> an optional avatar image you choose to upload.</li>
      <li><strong>Conversations:</strong> messages you send to your AI companion, in Conflict Mode, in the Community space, and in direct messages with other users.</li>
      <li><strong>Community content:</strong> text, polls, and voice messages you post or send to other users.</li>
      <li><strong>Support requests:</strong> anything you send us via email or in-app support.</li>
      <li><strong>Referral activity:</strong> your referral code and which users signed up using it.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section id="info-automatic">
    <h2>5. Information Collected Automatically</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Device &amp; usage data:</strong> device type, operating system, app version, and general usage patterns (e.g. number of messages sent), used to keep the App reliable and enforce fair-use limits.</li>
      <li><strong>Push notification token:</strong> a device identifier (via Firebase Cloud Messaging) used to deliver reminders and updates, if you allow notifications.</li>
      <li><strong>Purchase records:</strong> subscription status and purchase tokens from Google Play, used to grant and verify your plan.</li>
      <li><strong>Advertising identifiers:</strong> see the <a href="#ads">Advertising</a> section below.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section id="how-we-use">
    <h2>6. How We Use Your Information</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>To personalize your AI companion's responses based on what you've shared about yourself and your partner.</li>
      <li>To operate core features: chat, Conflict Mode, Daily Challenge, Community, direct messages, and Explore.</li>
      <li>To maintain and secure your account, including authentication and fraud prevention.</li>
      <li>To process subscription purchases and enforce plan-based limits.</li>
      <li>To respond to support requests.</li>
      <li>To send optional push notifications (e.g. streak reminders).</li>
      <li>To display advertisements to users on the Free plan.</li>
      <li>To improve the App's features and reliability over time.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section id="ai-processing">
    <h2>7. AI Processing &amp; Third-Party Providers</h2>
    <p>To provide the App's core functionality, certain information is shared with the following service providers, each acting on our behalf under their own security and data-handling commitments:</p>
    <table>
      <tr><th>Provider</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Data Involved</th></tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Google (Gemini API)</td>
        <td>Generates AI companion responses, Conflict Mode guidance, and Daily Challenge content</td>
        <td>Your onboarding/Customize answers, partner name, and message content — sent per-request, not used by Google to train models under our agreement</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Supabase</td>
        <td>Database, authentication, file storage, and serverless backend functions</td>
        <td>All account, profile, message, and purchase data</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Google Firebase (Cloud Messaging)</td>
        <td>Delivers push notifications</td>
        <td>Device push token only</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Google Play Billing</td>
        <td>Processes subscription payments</td>
        <td>Purchase tokens and subscription status — payment card details are handled entirely by Google and never reach our servers</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Google AdMob</td>
        <td>Serves advertisements to Free-plan users</td>
        <td>See <a href="#ads">Advertising</a> below</td>
      </tr>
    </table>
    <p>We do not sell your personal information to data brokers or use it for purposes unrelated to operating the App.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="ads">
    <h2>8. Advertising (Google AdMob)</h2>
    <p>Users on the <strong>Free plan</strong> see advertisements served through Google AdMob, including banner, interstitial, and rewarded video ads at specific points in the App (such as in Customize, Community, and Explore). <strong>Pro and Premium subscribers do not see ads.</strong></p>
    <ul>
      <li>AdMob may collect advertising identifiers (such as your device's advertising ID), IP address, and general device information to serve and measure ads.</li>
      <li>AdMob may use this information to personalize ads based on your interests, in accordance with Google's own privacy policy.</li>
      <li>You can review or reset your advertising ID, or opt out of personalized advertising, in your device's system settings (Android: Settings → Google → Ads).</li>
      <li>Google's use of advertising data is governed by the <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google Privacy Policy</a> and <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google's Partner Sites policy</a>.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section id="subscriptions">
    <h2>9. Subscriptions &amp; Payments</h2>
    <p>NIVORA offers optional paid subscription plans (Pro and Premium), billed monthly or yearly through <strong>Google Play Billing</strong>. When you subscribe:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Your payment is processed entirely by Google Play — we never receive or store your card details.</li>
      <li>We receive a purchase token and subscription status from Google, which we use to verify your purchase and grant your plan.</li>
      <li>Subscriptions renew automatically unless canceled through your Google Play account settings prior to the renewal date.</li>
      <li>Refunds are handled according to Google Play's refund policy; we do not directly process refunds.</li>
      <li>We receive automated renewal, cancellation, and expiration notifications from Google Play to keep your plan status accurate, even when the App is closed.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section id="notifications">
    <h2>10. Push Notifications</h2>
    <p>With your permission, we send push notifications for things like protecting a Daily Challenge streak. You can disable notifications at any time in the App's Profile settings, or through your device's system notification settings. Disabling notifications does not affect any other part of the App.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="data-safety">
    <h2>11. Data Safety Summary</h2>
    <p>This section summarizes our data practices in a format consistent with app store data safety disclosures.</p>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Data collected</h3>
      <p>Name, username, email-equivalent identifier, profile photo, relationship/onboarding answers, in-app messages, app activity, purchase history, device identifiers, and (if permitted) advertising identifiers and push notification tokens.</p>
      <h3>Data shared with third parties</h3>
      <p>Limited data is shared with the service providers listed in <a href="#ai-processing">Section 7</a> solely to operate the App's features (AI responses, hosting, notifications, payments, and advertising).</p>
      <h3>Data sold</h3>
      <p><strong>We do not sell your personal data.</strong></p>
      <h3>Security in transit</h3>
      <p>Data is encrypted in transit (HTTPS/TLS) between the App and our servers.</p>
      <h3>Data deletion</h3>
      <p>You may request deletion of your account and associated data at any time — see <a href="#rights">Your Rights &amp; Choices</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="security">
    <h2>12. Data Storage &amp; Security</h2>
    <p>Our database uses row-level security so that, by default, only you can access your own profile, messages, and answers — enforced at the database level, not just in the app. Access by our team is restricted to what's necessary to operate and support the App. No method of transmission or storage is 100% secure, and we cannot guarantee absolute security.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="retention">
    <h2>13. Data Retention</h2>
    <p>We retain your information for as long as your account remains active. If you request account deletion, we will delete or anonymize your personal data within a reasonable timeframe, except where retention is required for legal, security, or fraud-prevention purposes.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="rights">
    <h2>14. Your Rights &amp; Choices</h2>
    <p>Depending on where you live, you may have rights to access, correct, export, or delete your personal information, and to object to or restrict certain processing. To exercise any of these rights, contact us at <a href="mailto:support@inncatechnologies.com">support@inncatechnologies.com</a>. You can also directly manage or delete much of your profile information from within the App's Profile screen.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="sharing">
    <h2>15. Sharing of Information</h2>
    <p>We share information only:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>With the service providers described in Section 7, to the extent necessary to operate the App;</li>
      <li>When required to comply with applicable law, legal process, or governmental request;</li>
      <li>To protect the rights, property, or safety of Innca Technologies, our users, or the public;</li>
      <li>With your consent, or at your direction (for example, messages you choose to send to other users).</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section id="children">
    <h2>16. Children's Privacy</h2>
    <p>NIVORA is not directed at, and is not intended for use by, anyone under 18. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children. If you believe a child has provided us with personal information, please contact us so we can remove it.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="international">
    <h2>17. International Data Transfers</h2>
    <p>Your information may be processed and stored in countries other than your own, including by the service providers listed above. We take reasonable steps to ensure your data remains protected in accordance with this policy wherever it is processed.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="changes">
    <h2>18. Changes to This Policy</h2>
    <p>We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time to reflect changes in our practices or for legal, operational, or regulatory reasons. If we make material changes, we will take reasonable steps to notify you (such as an in-app notice) before the changes take effect. The "Last updated" date at the top of this page reflects the most recent revision.</p>
  </section>

